Parity unit : page:power-user/SqlPlayground   kind=page   web route=/power/sql
Web source  : web/src/features/power-user/pages/SqlPlaygroundPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/SqlPlaygroundPage/ (+ NavigationView registration, test, ledger)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- Layout mapping: the repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files). Every feature surface lives
  under apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent
  view), exactly as the sibling W7 ApiPlaygroundPage / StatusApiDocsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "Features/PowerUser/SqlPlaygroundPage.xaml + SqlPlaygroundPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real
  conventions. Namespace = TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.PowerUser (aligns with RouteGroup.PowerUser).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest declares NO API data sources ("renders from navigation params / local
  state"). The web page hand-writes read-only SQL against an install-wide-static curated catalog and never calls a
  SQL-execution endpoint. So the page is driven entirely by SqlPlaygroundPageViewModel over local state (the SQL
  text + the last Run message) with no generated-client call. The curated catalog is ported verbatim from the web
  CURATED_CATALOG (and mirrors the Go nlSqlPlaygroundCuratedCatalog) as SqlCatalog.Default; every numeric column is
  SI-canonical (distance_m / duration_s / energy_used_wh / avg_speed_mps / max_power_w), never a legacy unit suffix.
- Draft persistence (web localStorage['ai.sqlPlayground.draft']): represented by an injected
  ISqlPlaygroundDraftStore; the default InMemorySqlPlaygroundDraftStore.Shared reproduces survive-navigation drafts
  for the app session. VM.SetSql persists; the ctor loads the persisted draft.
- One data state (manifest: success). The page has no API source, so SqlPlaygroundProjection.Project always yields
  SqlPlaygroundState.Success and renders the editor + catalog (never a blank region, ADR-011). The deterministic
  Run notices (runEmpty / runUnavailable) are modelled as SqlRunMessageKind so the copy is re-resolved through the
  localizer on every projection (i18n re-render on language change) rather than frozen at click time.
- Panels (ADR-005), the manifest's two GlassPanel slots (web SqlPlaygroundPage.tsx, the two <GlassPanel>s):
  · GlassPanel1 = the manual SQL editor. A TsGlassPanel (SqlPlaygroundPage._editorPanel) hosting a PanelTitle
    (powerSql.editor.title), a multi-line TsTextarea (Hint = powerSql.editor.placeholder, AutomationName =
    powerSql.editor.label, spell-check off, rows≈10), a Run TsButton (Primary) + Clear TsButton (Secondary) both
    gated on canRun (web disabled={!canRun}), and a warning-toned run-message status line (web text-amber-300,
    role=status → AutomationLiveSetting.Polite).
  · GlassPanel2 = the curated schema catalog. A TsGlassPanel (_catalogPanel) hosting a PanelTitle
    (powerSql.catalog.title), an intro paragraph (powerSql.catalog.intro) and the sorted table list
    (BuildCatalogList → BuildTableCard → BuildColumnLine) from SqlCatalog.Sorted: each table a bordered card with a
    mono cyan name, a muted description and per-column "name · type — description" lines (mono emerald name).
  No hardcoded colours/typography — PageTitle/PanelTitle (Typography) + DisplayTokens (TsColorText*/Border,
  TsColorInfoBrush=cyan, TsColorSuccessBrush=emerald, TsColorWarningBrush=amber) drive light/dark/high-contrast
  from W1; mono = TypographyTokens.Mono.
- Scope note: the web page also mounts the opt-in AI drafter <AINLSqlPlayground onApply=…/> (wrapped in
  withAiFeature, absent in off-mode). The manifest scopes this unit to GlassPanel1+GlassPanel2 only; AINLSqlPlayground
  is a SEPARATE parity unit and is intentionally out of scope here (documented in SqlPlaygroundPage.cs).
- Navigation entry: RouteTable.cs already maps Page("PowerSqlPlayground","power/sql",RouteGroup.PowerUser)
  — unchanged. ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers the page factory next to the dev/power tooling cluster
  (new FeatureViews.PowerUser.SqlPlaygroundPage()). This page introduces NO new route.
- i18n (ADR-014): all eleven manifest keys (powerSql.title/intro, powerSql.editor.title/placeholder/label/run/clear/
  runEmpty/runUnavailable, powerSql.catalog.title/intro) are resolved through ILocalizer.GetString("powerSql.<key>",
  englishFallback) using the bare web key names with the verbatim web English defaults, exactly as the established
  ApiPlaygroundPage/StatusApiDocsPage precedent. The Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw catalog is AUTO-GENERATED
  ("do not edit by hand"); absent/locale keys resolve to the verbatim web English copy via the ShellLocalizer →
  ResourceLoader bridge (key '.'→'/'). Zero hardcoded UI text; zero hand-edit of the generated catalog.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page (title), the editor panel (Main landmark + editor title),
  the catalog panel (Custom landmark + catalog title); the TsTextarea carries the powerSql.editor.label Narrator
  name; the run message is an AutomationLiveSetting.Polite status region; each catalog table/column line carries a
  composed Narrator name; a Group automation peer; light/dark/high-contrast via the W1 tokens; TsTextarea/TsButton
  keyboard + pointer for free.
- Units (ADR-005/P1-S5): the page renders no measured quantities (it documents SI schema columns as text), so no
  unit conversion is involved; the catalog is SI-canonical by construction.

